        "client_msg_id": "394a05f8-e2c4-4972-981d-00d3dff4ca46",
        "text": "<@UCUSW7WVD> something you may run into with the single-file HTML/JS approach to be aware of is that some devices won\u2019t execute JS, or will only execute a subset of JS when reading the file directly from the file system as opposed to through a web server. This is a security measure to prevent folks from being able to easily embed and run malicious JS in all kinds of files (like PDFs :melting_face:)",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1737612150.216079",
        "parent_user_id": "UCUSW7WVD",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "vKOlP",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "user",
                                "user_id": "UCUSW7WVD"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " something you may run into with the single-file HTML/JS approach to be aware of is that some devices won\u2019t execute JS, or will only execute a subset of JS when reading the file directly from the file system as opposed to through a web server. This is a security measure to prevent folks from being able to easily embed and run malicious JS in all kinds of files (like PDFs "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "emoji",
                                "name": "melting_face",
                                "unicode": "1fae0"
                            },
